Third-party code
----------------
include/singlet/pileup/arriba_cascade.h, src/pipeline/arriba_cascade_cli.cpp and tests/cpp/test_arriba_cascade.cpp port the fusion
filter and scoring cascade of Arriba 2.5.1 (https://github.com/suhrig/arriba, commit 02bfd7d) to the engine's chimeric reads. They
are derived from these Arriba source files: annotation.cpp, annotation.t.hpp, common.hpp, arriba.cpp, fusions.cpp,
read_chimeric_alignments.cpp, read_stats.cpp, assembly.cpp, filter_duplicates.cpp, filter_uninteresting_contigs.cpp,
filter_proximal_read_through.cpp, filter_inconsistently_clipped.cpp, filter_homopolymer.cpp, filter_small_insert_size.cpp,
filter_long_gap.cpp, filter_same_gene.cpp, filter_hairpin.cpp, filter_mismatches.cpp, filter_low_entropy.cpp, filter_mismappers.cpp
(kmer_to_int), merge_adjacent_fusions.cpp, filter_multimappers.cpp, filter_relative_support.cpp, filter_non_coding_neighbors.cpp,
filter_intragenic_both_exonic.cpp, filter_min_support.cpp, filter_both_intronic.cpp, filter_in_vitro.cpp, recover_both_spliced.cpp,
select_best.cpp, filter_marginal_read_through.cpp, recover_many_spliced.cpp, filter_blacklisted_ranges.cpp, filter_short_anchor.cpp,
filter_end_to_end.cpp, filter_no_coverage.cpp, filter_genomic_support.cpp (assign_confidence) and output_fusions.cpp. Each ported
function keeps its Arriba name and cites its source file. Uhrig S, Ellermann J, Walther T, et al. Accurate and efficient detection
of gene fusions from RNA sequencing data. Genome Research 31:448-460 (2021), doi:10.1101/gr.257246.119. Arriba's license, which also
covers its database files, is vendored at data/fusion/arriba/LICENSE and reproduced here:

